{
  "id": "T-UISHOTS",
  "title": "DEV palette capture - the DEV lever 'uiview' opens the game's OWN main-menu screens (start column, Load Game, Options first tab, New Game sheet, the delete-save HudConfirm) through their own button onClick, plus our MP submenu; then the lobby redesign (2026-09-28) screens: Join a Game (plain + bad-port error), the lobby as host (DEV fill of 8), saved game, joiner, the Hosting port popup with the busy-port line, Connecting, Couldn't join, and the real 1-player host lobby. 'screenshot ui-<view>' captures each. Host only; the client idles at its main menu. NO save, no world load. Keep the host window unfocused but NOT minimised (a minimised window does not render). Fold 2026-09-28: 12-player lobby (scrollbar, long name, notice in the right column), thumb drag, track page, Escape on every window. Run at two sizes: normal, and BAMP_RIG_WINDOW=1280x720. MODS-GATE-1 (2026-09-29): the lobby's 'Different mods' row in both states + the saved-game variant, and the Couldn't join card with a mod refusal.",
  "preconditions": "Dev build with the 'uiview' lever (TestDrive.cs). At least one save on disk so Load Game lists something (the lever opens the window either way).",
